<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahdi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mahdi, meaning 'the rightly guided one', is a figure in Islamic belief expected to appear to restore justice and true religion. Claims to be the Mahdi have legitimised several movements. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-tumart">Ibn Tumart</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> movement, was proclaimed Mahdi, and the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>, Abdallah al-Mahdi, also drew on Mahdist expectations.</p></div>
